94
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:13,740
..."Who are you wearing? You look fabulous!"

95
00:06:15,330 --> 00:06:18,410
Might I suggest watching a little more ESPN...

96
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:20,000
...and a little less E!

97
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:23,790
Okay. Who wore those?

98
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:25,210
Uh...

99
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:28,920
- Well, uh, this one's Tom Brokaw.     - Not bad.

100
00:06:29,090 --> 00:06:31,930
This one is, uh, Paul O'Neil.

101
00:06:33,050 --> 00:06:34,600
Who's that?

102
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:39,850
He plays for the Yankees. Seriously, ESPN.

103
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:43,310
Just once in a while. Have it on in the background.

104
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:48,280
Ooh, this one was Pierce Brosnan.

105
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:49,490
- Pierce Brosnan?     - Uh-huh.

106
00:06:49,650 --> 00:06:50,950
Are you serious?

107
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:52,240
007？
007?

108
00:06:52,410 --> 00:06:57,620
This is James Bond's tux? Oh, I have to get married in James Bond's tux.

109
00:06:57,790 --> 00:06:59,410
Ha, ha. It's a pretty cool tux.

110
00:06:59,580 --> 00:07:02,750
Ah, it's not just that. I would be England's most powerful weapon.

111
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:08,880
A jet-setting heartbreaker on Her Majesty's secret service.

112
00:07:09,050 --> 00:07:12,800
A man who fears no one, with a license to kill.

113
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,680
Would Monica let me wear this?

114
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:24,860
We should really learn how to play the real way.

115
00:07:25,110 --> 00:07:26,230
I like our way.

116
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:28,400
- Ah!     - Hey, hey!

117
00:07:28,570 --> 00:07:30,110
Chess!

118
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:34,700
- Nice move.     - Yeah.

119
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,620
- Hey.     - Hey.

120
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:41,830
I hooked Ross and Chandler up with tuxedos. Do you need one?

121
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,210
No, I'm not wearing a tux.

122
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:48,500
- What are you gonna wear?     - Multi-colored robes.

123
00:07:48,670 --> 00:07:50,260
Ooh, and maybe a hat.

124
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:52,670
- Huh. Does Monica know about this?     - No.

125
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:55,550
Can I please be there when you tell her?

126
00:07:57,760 --> 00:08:00,220
Hey, Rach, you want to go to a movie tonight?

127
00:08:00,390 --> 00:08:02,680
Oh, I can't. I'm having dinner with Melissa.

128
00:08:02,850 --> 00:08:04,020
Can I come?

129
00:08:05,770 --> 00:08:08,940
I won't talk. You'll just hear my video camera.

130
00:08:09,110 --> 00:08:12,070
- What? What's going on?     - Can I tell her?

131
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:14,910
Do you want what happened, or Joey's lewd version?

132
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:17,240
- Joey's.      - Okay.

133
00:08:17,410 --> 00:08:18,660
Okay, come on.

134
00:08:18,830 --> 00:08:20,410
I had this college friend...

135
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:24,580
...and I made the mistake of telling Joey that one time...

136
00:08:24,830 --> 00:08:28,460
...she and I, you know, kissed a little bit.

137
00:08:28,630 --> 00:08:29,670


138
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,840
Yeah, I'm sure that happened.

139
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:36,090
- It did.      - Sure.

140
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:40,600
Hey, heh. It happened.

141
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:46,600
Yeah, it was senior year. It was after the Sigma Chi luau...

142
00:08:46,770 --> 00:08:49,110
...and Melissa and I got very drunk.

143
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:53,440
And we ended up kissing. For several minutes.

144
00:08:53,610 --> 00:08:56,950
Which means she had a couple spritzers and a peck on the cheek.

145
00:08:58,570 --> 00:09:01,580
- Why are you taking this away from me? - Ugh.

146
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,450
Why is it so hard for you to believe?

147
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:08,210
Okay. I just didn't know that you were a lesbian.

148
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:20,010
I'm not saying that I'm a lesbian. I'm just saying that this happened.

149
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:24,890
It just seems pretty wild. And you're... You know, so...

150
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:26,940
...vanilla.

151
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:32,020
Vanilla? I'm not vanilla. I do lots of crazy things.

152
00:09:32,230 --> 00:09:35,740
I mean, I got drunk and married in Vegas.

153
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,200
To Ross.

154
00:09:38,530 --> 00:09:40,410
If you don't believe me...

155
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,950
...just come with me to dinner tonight and she'll tell you.

156
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:47,040
Okay. Because I can't picture it.

157
00:09:47,290 --> 00:09:50,170
You should get inside my head.

158
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:55,960
- Hey.     - Hey.

159
00:09:56,130 --> 00:09:57,840
Guess what I got for your wedding?

160
00:09:58,010 --> 00:10:00,550
A freakishly thin date with a hanger for a head?

161
00:10:01,850 --> 00:10:05,720
Rachel hooked me up with a tux. But not just any tux.

162
00:10:05,890 --> 00:10:07,770
Batman's tux!

163
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,770
